  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "A Paraguayan judge has ordered former president Santiago Peña transferred to Viñas Cué military prison pending trial on charges of criminal association, breach of trust, and misuse of public office.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 6 November 2026, the Senate removed Santiago Peña from office and revoked his constitutional immunity, and Vice President Pedro Alliana assumed the presidency.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385819313:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The crisis is an ongoing financial and political one, triggered by the regulatory intervention and shutdown of Ueno Bank, the country's largest digital financial institution.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385819313:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On 9 November, President Pedro Alliana appointed economist Jorge Schreiner to lead the central bank after Ueno Bank's collapse, and the Senate approved the appointment.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-09:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:32Z",
      "text": "By 11 November, the Central Bank of Paraguay reported providing partial refunds to 1,812,348 eligible Ueno Bank depositors.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-11:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "The reports place the Viñas Cué military prison in Paraguay, where the former president was ordered transferred.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:49Z",
      "text": "The crisis began on 3 November 2026, and it is recorded as taking place in Paraguay.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q142059724:P580",
        "wd:Q142059724:P17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:00:59Z",
      "text": "The report was published by Reuters.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-16:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-16T00:01:07Z",
      "text": "This explainer draws on Wikipedia's Current events portal for 2026 November 9, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews, and Wikidata, and each statement links to its evidence.",
      "cites": [
